<title>USA: Weekend Box Office Chart -- September 13-15.</title>
<headline>Weekend Box Office Chart -- September 13-15.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are final data for the top 10 movies at the September 13-15 holiday weekend box office, according to Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc.</p>
<p>    Film		    Three-Day Gross     Cumulative Gross</p>
<p> 1. Maximum Risk	     $ 5,612,707	 $   ----</p>
<p> 2. Fly Away Home	    $ 4,708,044	 $   ----</p>
<p> 3. Bulletproof		$ 4,102,845	 $ 11,886,800</p>
<p> 4. Tin Cup		    $ 3,327,083	 $ 46,732,867</p>
<p> 5. The Rich Man's Wife    $ 3,132,151	 $   ----</p>
<p> 6. First Kid		  $ 3,112,013	 $ 17,437,678</p>
<p> 7. A Time To Kill	   $ 2,838,127	 $101,002,684</p>
<p> 8. The Spitfire Grill     $ 2,433,327	 $  7,505,043</p>
<p> 9. Independence Day	 $ 2,064,424	 $288,445,301</p>
<p> 10 Jack			 $ 2,009,749	 $ 52,029,384</p>
<p>NOTE: &quot;Maximum Risk&quot;, &quot;Fly Away Home&quot; and &quot;The Spitfire Grill&quot; are released by Columbia Pictures, a unit of Sony Corp. &quot;Bulletproof&quot; is released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd. &quot;Tin Cup&quot; and &quot;A Time To Kill&quot; are released by Time Warner Inc's Warner Bros. &quot;First Kid&quot;, &quot;The Rich Man's Wife&quot; and &quot;Jack&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Independence Day&quot; is released by News Corp.'s 20th Century Fox.</p>
